NODE id=matrix/router/internal/proxy.Handler.forward kind=method
  digest=b3:aabb3f661f961f69ceace901b64a57e4327453ee0b772130f0e694d0561d7a69 file=router/internal/proxy/proxy.go range=220:316 lang=go exported=false byte_range=7609:11680
  sig=func (h *Handler) forward(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, sub string, ref provision.Ref)
  doc=forward is the wake-then-proxy core: wake the environment, wait for\nthe in-machine daemon to accept connections, then reverse-proxy the\nrequest to it. Split from ServeHTTP so the wake path is exercisable\nend-to-end without a Postgres row behind it.
